<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1926a, 1926b), Zamir (1976) & Sherman (1981) minimum-work vascular cube law & arterial branching angles — Model fidelity to source: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements Murray's (1926a) Poiseuille + metabolic power functional P(r), stationarity radius r*, and exact wall shear stress invariance tau_w = sqrt(eta*b) = 8.2189 dyn/cm^2 across 7 vascular generations (L100-147, L284-338), plus Murray's (1926b) full asymmetric bifurcation angle laws cos(theta_1) and cos(theta_2) alongside Zamir's (1976) surface-drag (90 deg), Steiner's length-minimizing (120 deg), and Da Vinci's area-preserving (gamma=2) negative controls (L154-279, L340-421). Backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 `sorry`s) in `Loop_052_vascular_cube_law_branching.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1926a, 1926b), Zamir (1976) & Sherman (1981) minimum-work vascular cube law & arterial branching angles — Morphometric validation: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` reports 8 quantitative morphometrics with reference values, uncertainty/dispersion statistics (RMSE, Pearson r, p-value, SD, CV), and negative-control ablation deltas (L891-985): empirical human retinal junctions J01-J08 achieve total-angle RMSE = 0.134 deg and branch-angle Pearson r = 0.9999 (p = 2.4e-26), cube-law conservation ratio (r_1^3+r_2^3)^(1/3)/r_0 = 0.9956 ± 0.0033 (CV = 0.0033) vs Da Vinci gamma=2 control 1.1091 (+11.4% bias and +134.8% excess tree power), and segmented fundus Y-junction angle mean = 79.28 deg (N = 19)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
