<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1926a, 1926b), Zamir (1976) & Sherman (1981) minimum-work vascular cube law & arterial branching angles — MorphoEval overall 90.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2 remediated) evaluation of `1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py` (90.9/100, up from 51.4/100 in Pass 1; +39.5 overall). The remediated script implements Murray's (1926a) Poiseuille + metabolic cost functional P(r), stationarity partition P_met(r*)/P_visc(r*) = 2.0, scale-invariant wall shear stress tau_w = sqrt(eta*b) = 8.2189 dyn/cm^2 across all 7 Sherman (1981) arteriole generations, and Murray's (1926b) full asymmetric bifurcation cosine laws cos(theta_1), cos(theta_2) across alpha = r_2/r_1 in (0, 1]; compares against competing Zamir (1976) surface-drag (90 deg), Steiner length-minimum (120 deg), and Da Vinci area-preserving (gamma=2, +134.8% excess tree power) ablation controls; segments N=19 Y-junctions on the SHA-256-verified human retinal fundus specimen (`retinal_vasculature_specimen.jpg`, mean angle 79.28 deg, cube-law ratio 0.917, tortuosity B/A = 1.015x); and is backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_052_vascular_cube_law_branching.lean`. Overall 90.6/100 (faithfulness 89.7, reproducibility 92.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 87, Parameter expressivity 89, Morphometric validation 89, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/vascular_cube_law_branching_comparison.png: rendered output of 1959-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching.py at 8871db0, image/png, 807479 B, 2537×1537 px, artifact_sha256 6f5c640c92a289282dfe1e11d26a302fc561053ef8d7c679ab2ac12c8e5202a0 (sha256 6f5c640c92a289282dfe1e11d26a302fc561053ef8d7c679ab2ac12c8e5202a0), spec_fingerprint d50b49ef447bf68e29d604bf8fac7d65aec5afb9d6827a3f7ef26e8dd37a2ab8. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d50b49ef447bf68e29d604bf8fac7d65aec5afb9d6827a3f7ef26e8dd37a2ab8; artifact_sha256: 6f5c640c92a289282dfe1e11d26a302fc561053ef8d7c679ab2ac12c8e5202a0; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/retinal_vasculature_specimen.jpg=bc548d4150e070a5..., datasets/vascular_cube_law_branching/vascular_cube_law_branching_reference.json=6d1761f2e01e4fa7...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-vascular-cube-law-branching-audit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Extend 2D retinal vascular tree synthesis to 3D curved hemispherical retinal cup geometry with coupled arteriovenous interdigitation.",
        "remediation needed: Incorporate non-Newtonian Fahraeus-Lindqvist apparent blood viscosity eta(r) in pre-capillary arterioles (r < 25 um) to quantify the shift in optimal exponent from gamma = 3.0 toward gamma ≈ 2.7." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.06e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-vascular-cube-law-branching-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
